.TH CBMAP_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_create \- create a BST map with default settings
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

cbmap cbmap_create(ccol_data_type key_type, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a self-balancing binary search tree map (AVL tree) with default
memory management and default comparison based on the key type.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
key_type  Type of the keys stored in the map
err       Optional pointer to receive error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to newly created BST map on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Default comparison for char: this platform's own native char comparison
  (signed or unsigned, matching however char behaves on this platform)
Default comparison for the other signed integer types: signed integer
  comparison
Default comparison for unsigned integer types: unsigned integer comparison
Default comparison for float/double/long double: numeric comparison; a NaN
  key sorts as greater than every non-NaN key and equal to every other NaN
  key
Default comparison for ccol_string: strcmp-equivalent lexicographic order
Map maintains AVL balance: |height(left) - height(right)| <= 1
All operations are O(log n) for balanced tree
Map must be destroyed with cbmap_destroy() when done
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create_full (3),
.BR cbmap_destroy (3)
